{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"gentile-greedsome-gavial","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEvery execution opens its pull request against one branch for the whole platform. `TemporalStarter.start` at `services/orchestration/intake_runtime.py:49` sets `base = self._settings.github_default_base_branch`, and that value reaches the pull request unchanged, through `DraftPullRequestInput.base` at `draft_pull_request.py:213` into `PullRequestInput.base` at line 742.\n\nA per-ticket base is already modelled and already dead. `IntakeStart.base` is declared at `intake_reconciler.py:44`, the only construction site at line 365 never sets it, and `TemporalStarter.start` overwrites it with the setting regardless.\n\nThe consequence is that work depending on an unmerged change cannot be automated. A ticket whose fix only makes sense on top of another open pull request has to target the shared default branch, so its diff either carries the parent change as noise or does not apply at all. This blocks the pilot against `archive-massgov-pfml`, where the accessibility fix for ticket `98b3-e6e7-689f-4ae0` needs the Storybook story added by pull request 14 on branch `joeoakhart/PFMLPB-33758` to be exercised at all.\n\n## Approach\n\nLet a ticket declare its base branch, and honour that declaration at intake.\n\nThe declaration travels as a `base:<branch>` label. Labels are the one ticket attribute both sources already normalise to a common shape, so a single parser serves both backends without a second code path. `rebar_stored_payload` maps rebar tags to `labels` at `rebar_backend.py:97`, and `normalize_issue` maps Jira labels to the same key at `jira/normalize.py:70`. A client on either backend declares a stacked base the same way, which is why this beats a rebar-only field or a new setting. A setting is wrong regardless of backend, because the base varies per ticket while a setting is per deployment.\n\nThe declaration is an override. `github_default_base_branch` stays authoritative for every ticket that declares nothing, so existing behaviour is unchanged.\n\nThe failure mode is closed. `remote_head` returns an empty string for a branch that does not exist on the remote, and an empty `base_sha` is not inert. It is the workspace checkout commit at `draft_pull_request.py:426` and the fallback gate commit at line 618, so a mistyped branch would produce an execution rooted at no known commit. A declared base that does not resolve therefore holds the ticket and alerts through the existing unroutable path. Falling back to the default would silently target the wrong branch and produce a pull request whose diff is not the one the ticket asked for.\n\nThe hold is raised as a typed error from the starter and caught around the ledger call in `_start`, so one unroutable ticket does not abort the rest of the intake pass.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `services/orchestration/intake_base.py` is new and holds `declared_base` and `UnresolvableBaseBranch`.\n- `services/orchestration/intake_reconciler.py` gains `base_branch` on `IntakeCandidate`, populates it in both adapters, passes it as `IntakeStart.base`, and holds the ticket when the starter reports the base unresolvable. `IntakeStart.base` defaults to an empty string rather than `\"main\"`, so the setting remains the only place the default branch is named.\n- `services/orchestration/intake_runtime.py` honours `start.base` when set and raises `UnresolvableBaseBranch` when `remote_head` returns empty.\n- `docs/` documents the label convention, the override precedence, and the hold behaviour.\n- Tests: `tests/unit/test_intake_base.py` is new.\n\n## Grounded assumptions\n\n- The workflow already supports an arbitrary base. `DraftPullRequestInput.base` at `draft_pull_request.py:213` is passed to `PullRequestInput.base` at line 742 with no reference to the setting, so only the selection at intake is missing.\n- Both ticket sources expose labels under the same key. `rebar_backend.py:97` writes `\"labels\": list(ticket.get(\"tags\") or [])` and `jira/normalize.py:42` writes `\"labels\": list(self.labels)`, so one parser reading `stored_payload[\"labels\"]` covers both.\n- `IntakeStart.base` has no current effect. The only construction site is `intake_reconciler.py:365` and it omits `base`, so changing its default from `\"main\"` to `\"\"` cannot alter any existing execution.\n- An unresolved branch yields an empty string rather than an error. `remote_head` at `intake_runtime.py:25` returns `proc.stdout.split()[0] if proc.stdout.strip() else \"\"`, and `git ls-remote` exits 0 for a ref that does not match, so `check=True` does not catch it.\n- Holding is the established response to an unroutable ticket. `route_candidate` calls `_hold` at `intake_reconciler.py:249` when `resolution.routable` is false, alerting the operator and recording a hold.\n- An exception from the starter would otherwise abort the pass. `PostgresSideEffectLedger.run_once` at `idempotency.py:108` does not catch exceptions from the effect, so the error must be caught in `_start`.\n- The branch this pilot targets exists. `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/joeoakhart/PFMLPB-33758` against `archive-massgov-pfml` returns `b0117d05d8`, the head of pull request 14.\n\n## Testing\n\nHappy path: a candidate carrying `base:feature-x` starts a workflow whose `base` is `feature-x` and whose `base_sha` is the remote head of that branch.\n\nFailure and edge paths: a candidate with no `base:` label uses `github_default_base_branch`. A candidate declaring a branch that does not resolve is held with a reason naming the branch, and no workflow starts. An empty value such as `base:` is treated as no declaration. Two conflicting `base:` labels hold the ticket rather than picking one arbitrarily. A label merely beginning with the prefix, such as `baseline`, is not a declaration, and the prefix is matched case-sensitively because branch names are. A branch name containing a colon keeps everything after the first colon. A held ticket does not stop the pass, verified with one unresolvable candidate and a second that still starts.\n\nLive end to end: the pilot ticket for `98b3-e6e7-689f-4ae0` opens a pull request against `archive-massgov-pfml` whose base is `joeoakhart/PFMLPB-33758`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A candidate carrying a `base:<branch>` label starts a workflow with that branch as `base` and with `base_sha` resolved from that branch, verified by `tests/unit/test_intake_base.py`.\n- [ ] A candidate with no `base:` label starts a workflow with `github_default_base_branch` as `base`, verified by the same module.\n- [ ] A declared branch that does not resolve on the remote holds the ticket with a reason naming the branch and starts no workflow, verified by a reconciler test asserting on `IntakeReport.held` and on the absence of any `IntakeStartRecord`.\n- [ ] A held ticket does not prevent other candidates in the same pass from starting, verified by a test with two candidates.\n- [ ] An empty declaration such as `base:` falls back to the default branch, and a label such as `baseline` is not read as a declaration, verified by two tests.\n- [ ] Two conflicting `base:` labels hold the ticket rather than selecting one, verified by a test.\n- [ ] A declared branch containing a colon is preserved in full, verified by a test.\n- [ ] Both `candidate_from_rebar` and `candidate_from_jira` populate `base_branch` from labels, verified by one test per adapter.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A live run of the pilot ticket for `98b3-e6e7-689f-4ae0` opens a pull request against `archive-massgov-pfml` whose base branch is `joeoakhart/PFMLPB-33758`.\n  provenance: environment=local-colima-k3s; principal=joeoakhart; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the pilot executes the shipped intake and workflow path against the client repository over the same Temporal path a deployment uses\n- [ ] Documentation names the `base:<branch>` label convention, states that the setting applies when no label is present, and states that an unresolvable declared branch holds the ticket.\n- [ ] `ruff check services tests scripts adapters` exits 0.","id":"beea-372a-e874-4b54","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"ADEVX-102 Honour a ticket-declared base branch at intake"},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789493335227491001,"uuid":"e5eadf93-de3e-4f1a-bb44-02813e08ac9e"}